EKS: EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service) is AWS-managed Kubernetes.

In simple words
------------------
EKS = Kubernetes + AWS management
AWS runs the Kubernetes control plane for you.
----
What we are creating
---------------------
1 EKS Cluster (Control Plane – managed by AWS)
1 Node Group
2 Worker Nodes (EC2)
IAM Roles
Cluster Role
Node Group Role
VPC + Subnets (new or existing)
------------------------------------
STEP 1: Create IAM Role for EKS Cluster
------
1️⃣ Go to IAM → Roles → Create role
Trusted entity: AWS service
Use case: EKS
Select: EKS – Cluster
------------------------
2️⃣ Attach these policies (MANDATORY):
✅ AmazonEKSClusterPolicy
👉 Click Next → Name
Role name: EKS-Cluster-Role
Create role
📌 PurposeThis role allows EKS control plane to talk to AWS services.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
🔹 STEP 2: Create IAM Role for Worker Nodes (Node Group)
----------
1️⃣ IAM → Roles → Create role
Trusted entity: AWS service
Use case: EC2
2️⃣ Attach these policies (VERY IMPORTANT):
✅ AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy
✅ AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy
✅ AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly
3️⃣ Name the role:
EKS-Node-Group-Role
Create role
📌 Purpose
This role allows:
Worker nodes to join cluster
Pull images from ECR
Communicate with control plane
