Why worker nodes in private subnet
----------------------------------
✅ Short interview answer ( realtime)
Worker nodes are placed in private subnets to prevent direct internet access, improve security, and follow enterprise security standards.
EXAMPLE:
--------
User (Internet)
   ↓
Application Load Balancer (Public Subnet)
   ↓
Kubernetes Service / Ingress
   ↓
Worker Nodes (Private Subnet)
   ↓
Pods (Application)
🚫 Users never talk directly to worker nodes
--------------------------------------------------
🔹 MAIN REASONS (Point-to-Point)
1️⃣ Security (MOST IMPORTANT)
If worker nodes are PUBLIC ❌
Anyone can try:
SSH
Port scanning
Attacks
Node IP is exposed to internet
----------------------------------
If worker nodes are PRIVATE ✅
No public IP
No direct inbound traffic
Only ALB can reach them
📌 Banking, insurance, fintech → mandatory
------------------------------------------
Best answer:
“Technically yes, but in real-time production we never do that. Worker nodes are always placed in private subnets for security and compliance.”
