1) aws configure
enter: AWS Access Key
      AWS Secret Key
      Region (example: ap-south-1)
      Output format: json

Tip (Real production practice):
---------------------------------
Instead of aws configure, many companies attach an IAM role to the Bastion EC2 instance
so AWS CLI works automatically without storing keys.

Create IAM Role for Bastion Server
---------------------------------------
Go to AWS Console → IAM → Roles → Create Role
Select:
Trusted entity → EC2
Click Next
Attach policies like:
Common policies for EKS access:
----------------------------------
AmazonEKSClusterPolicy
AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy
AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly
Give role name: bastion-eks-role
Create the role.

Attach Role to Bastion EC2
----------------------------
EC2 → Instances → Select Bastion Instance
Actions
 → Security
 → Modify IAM Role
Select the role: which i have created
save.
Now the EC2 instance has temporary AWS credentials automatically.

Verify IAM Role from Bastion Server
------------------------------------
aws sts get-caller-identity

